Description: Let PBSP and PVP2 work on consecutive H.264 frames at once
 The VP2 decoder ran each frame through PBSP and then PVP2 with one set of
 buffers and one semaphore, so the CPU waited for a frame to finish before
 it queued the next, and the two engines never overlapped. Frames now
 cycle through three slots, each with its own bitstream, vpring, VP
 parameters and semaphore, and PVP2 gets its own scratch area instead of
 the tail of mbring, so no buffer is shared between PBSP on one frame and
 PVP2 on the ones before. The engines write a semaphore once they are done
 with a frame, after their channel has moved on, so the semaphores count
 up and each channel waits for its engine's write: the channel's fence
 then means the engine is done, before the CPU refills a slot or the kernel
 moves a buffer.
